From 55436ba3bf17ac4a587d856f7d80682982a391ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woksin <sindrewilting@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:08:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] Add MongoDB writer fence: gate records, fenced batch
 executor and unknown-commit resolution

Prototype for #5225. A fenced batch runs in one transaction that first writes
the gate record expecting the owner's epoch, then the batch's writes, then a
receipt. Revocation bumps the epoch in a transaction and so serializes against
admitted batches. An unknown commit result is resolved by an unconditional gate
write plus a receipt read in one transaction, never by a blind retry.
